  "ingredients": [
    "2 cups all-purpose flour",
    "1 teaspoon salt",
    "0.5 cup shortening, chilled",
    "0.5 cup cold water",
    "2 apples - peeled, cored and diced",
    "0.25 cup white sugar, or to taste",
    "0.125 teaspoon ground cinnamon, or to taste",
    "1 quart oil for frying, or as needed"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "To make the pastry: Sift flour and salt together in a large bowl. Cut in shortening with 2 knives or a pastry blender until mixture resembles coarse crumbs.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/9DEIDL-6sOJuwOizmZOor-MFLyQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/12680-fried-apple-pies-ddmfs-Step-1-9337309093394a618519f021aad840dd.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/12680/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add cold water, 1 tablespoon at a time, tossing with a fork, until flour mixture is moistened. Do not add more water than you need: when you squeeze a handful of moistened pastry mixture, it should form a ball. Wrap in plastic wrap and refrigerate for 30 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/yWJTcTyYXQxiu-Pin62cUdXX5qI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/12680-fried-apple-pies-ddmfs-Step-2-c3b102a2a03d477aa6dfb2cc7eca61f8.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/12680/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "To make the filling: Place apples in a saucepan. Combine sugar and cinnamon; pour over apples and toss to coat. Cook, covered, in a saucepan on low heat until soft; mash with a fork to make thick applesauce. Set aside to cool.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/hDXdqclG7o57rTNlQUSHow-9izo=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/12680-fried-apple-pies-ddmfs-Step-4-42e9808b8ca7423e9231545c09cbbe0f.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/12680/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Roll dough on a lightly floured surface to 1/8-inch thick; cut out eight 4-inch rounds with a large cookie cutter.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/2hVswxfevePu8RZNHdcy4kB3VxE=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/12680-fried-apple-pies-ddmfs-Step-5-e0f23dea96814c05978feac03c38bf3a.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/12680/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place 1 heaping tablespoon of applesauce in the center of each pastry round. Moisten edges with cold water, fold in half, and press the edge with a fork to seal. Repeat with remaining pastry and filling.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/BaHJxqcOKikYpYAyeNnwIFAphFE=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/12680-fried-apple-pies-ddmfs-Step-7-53468be41cc5498d94abbdfa84bd73bb.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/12680/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat oil in a deep fryer or large saucepan to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Lower pies carefully into the hot oil in batches. Fry until golden brown, about 2 to 3 minutes on each side. Transfer to a paper towel-lined plate to drain. Repeat with remaining pies.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/e3f5pFMOY2_Az72ZPVCpyIWNmx0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/12680-fried-apple-pies-ddmfs-Step-8-d9d0ffbbecba4976a6d4efdca4c1155a.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/12680/step_07.webp"
    }
  ],
